      "side": 1,
      "message": "Could the new-Child-SA caller also honor this error before appending a child? For an authenticated CREATE_CHILD_SA request with a matching MODP group, a zero KE and no REKEY_SA notify, this branch frees `rekey-\u003er_proposal` and returns 0. `ikev2_process_create_child_sa_req()` then frees `proposal` but leaves it in `sa-\u003enew_child[0].i_proposal`; the node\u0027s `new_child` branch unconditionally copies that dangling pointer into `sa-\u003echilds`. Unlike the rekey branch, it never checks `notify_type`. A subsequent Child-SA dump dereferences the freed proposal, and SA cleanup frees it again. Please guard child creation on successful DH/proposal negotiation and retain only the error response on failure.",
      "tag": "prview:898577ec13c2636e6a72af3b46b1af3d:59234c1c44e48738b38b80f64dd17e77b19155a6",
