      "writtenOn": "2026-11-04T17:57:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Could this failure exit free the temporary SA and remove the pending initiator entry before dispatch? `ikev2_complete_sa_data()` has already moved the nonce, DH private key, identities, authentication data, children and saved request out of `sai` into stack-local `sa0`. This `goto` skips `ikev2_sa_free_all_vec(sa0)` below, and `dispatch0` only deletes DELETED/NOTIFY_AND_DELETE SAs, so these allocations are lost. It also leaves `sai-\u003einit_response_received \u003d 1`; the pending-SA loop skips it forever and subsequent valid responses cannot pass the CAS. A zero MODP KE therefore leaks the exchange\u0027s allocations and leaves initiation stuck until explicit cleanup.",
